Dear Quality Assurance Team,

I am writing to raise an urgent complaint regarding a consignment of
Amlodipine Besylate Tablets IP 5 mg received at Sterling Hospitals,
Ahmedabad on 16 July 2026.

During a routine dispensing check our pharmacist noted that the blister
foils inside three cartons of batch ZPL-2506-0412 are printed as
"Amlodipine Besylate Tablets IP 10 mg", while the outer carton and the
shipper label both state 5 mg. The tablets in the affected blisters are
also visibly larger than those in the remaining cartons of the same batch.

Quantity affected: 3 cartons (90 tablets).
Manufacturing date printed on the carton: 01/2026
Expiry date printed on the carton: 12/2027

No tablets from the affected cartons have been dispensed to any patient.
All three cartons have been segregated and placed in quarantine in our
pharmacy store, and the remainder of the batch has been placed on hold
pending your response.

Given the potential for a dosing error we consider this a serious matter
and request your urgent investigation, along with written confirmation of
the disposition of the remaining stock.

Kind regards,

